Task 1: Registration Form Design
Objective
Create a registration form using HTML and CSS.



registration.html
<!DOCTYPE html><html><head>    <title>Registration Form</title></head><body><form>    <h2>Registration Form</h2>    Name:    <input type="text" name="name"><br><br>    Email:    <input type="email" name="email"><br><br>    Mobile:    <input type="text" name="mobile"><br><br>    Password:    <input type="password" name="password"><br><br>    Confirm Password:    <input type="password" name="confirm_password"><br><br>    <input type="submit" value="Register"></form></body></html>
Line-by-Line Explanation
<!DOCTYPE html>
Tells browser this is an HTML5 page.
<html>
Starts HTML document.
<head>
Contains page information.
<title>Registration Form</title>
Browser tab title.
<body>
Visible page content.
<form>
Starts the form.
<input type="text">
User enters name.
<input type="email">
User enters email.
<input type="password">
Password field hides text.
<input type="submit">
Submit button.

Task 2: Registration Form Validation
validation.js



function validateForm(){    var name = document.getElementById("name").value;    var email = document.getElementById("email").value;    var mobile = document.getElementById("mobile").value;    var password = document.getElementById("password").value;    if(name=="")    {        alert("Name Required");        return false;    }    if(email=="")    {        alert("Email Required");        return false;    }    if(mobile.length!=10)    {        alert("Mobile must be 10 digits");        return false;    }    if(password.length<6)    {        alert("Password minimum 6 characters");        return false;    }    return true;}
Explanation
var name
Stores entered name.
if(name=="")
Checks empty name.
alert()
Shows error message.
return false
Stops form submission.

